0001 — compiler/decl.rs: property declaration rules of php-src master
(zend_compile_prop_decl).

* Readonly properties may have a default value (RFC "Allow Readonly Property
  Defaults", php-src a2640aebc91): the "Readonly property %s::$%s cannot have
  default value" error is gone.
* A readonly class makes *every* property readonly, static ones included, so
  `readonly class Foo { public static int $bar; }` now fails with "Static
  property Foo::$bar cannot be readonly" (it was silently accepted).
* `final` is allowed on properties without hooks (PHP 8.4); the old
  "Cannot declare property final, the final modifier is allowed only on
  methods, classes, and properties with hooks" error is removed (the FINAL
  flag was already carried into PropDecl, so Reflection isFinal()/
  getModifiers()/__toString() report it).
* Check order and texts as in master: enum, final+private, interface
  (final / protected-private / explicit abstract), then for a property
  without hooks "Interfaces may only include hooked properties" and
  "Only hooked properties may be declared abstract".

Fixes: Zend/tests/readonly_props/readonly_with_default{,_asymmetric_visibility,
_inheritance,_interface_get_only}, readonly_trait_match, readonly_clone_success1,
unset; Zend/tests/readonly_classes/readonly_class_property3,
readonly_with_property_default{,_trait}; Zend/tests/property_hooks/
abstract_prop_without_hooks, final_prop_promoted_{2,3,4}(with 0003);
Zend/tests/errmsg/errmsg_037; tests/classes/interface_member; ext/reflection
ReflectionProperty_{isFinal,getModifiers_basic,readonly_with_default,
toString_002}, ReflectionClass_toString_009, final_property_indicated.

